{"id": "phn:mutal-alvars-fourth-presence", "lineage": "lin:alvar", "kind": "state", "description": "In the dark, cramped vestibule at Tirukkōvalūr the three first Āḻvārs felt a fourth, unseen presence pressing among them — the Lord — before the lamps of verse were lit.", "source": "src:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati", "ref": "Mutal Āḻvārs", "rests_on": ["tea:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati:mutal-alvars"], "stage": "realized (the tradition's account)", "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:peyalvar-vision-of-sri", "lineage": "lin:alvar", "kind": "vision", "description": "By the light of the others' lamps Pēyāḻvār saw Śrī, the golden form, the sun-like hue, the discus and the conch in the ocean-hued Lord.", "source": "src:munram-tiruvantati", "ref": "1", "rests_on": ["tea:munram-tiruvantati:1"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:nammalvar-sixteen-years-absorption", "lineage": "lin:alvar", "kind": "state", "description": "From birth Nammāḻvār neither cried nor fed and sat silent in the hollow of the tamarind tree at Kurukūr for sixteen years, absorbed in the Lord, until Madhurakavi's question drew his first words.", "source": "src:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati", "ref": "Nammāḻvār", "rests_on": ["tea:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati:nammalvar-madhurakavi"], "stage": "the tradition's account", "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:parankusa-nayaki-lovesickness", "lineage": "lin:alvar", "kind": "bodily", "description": "The love-sick girl (the Āḻvār as heroine) knows no sleep night or day, bails out her tears with her hands, joins her palms at the names of the conch and discus, and melts — as her mother describes her to the Lord of Śrīraṅgam.", "source": "src:tiruvaymoli", "ref": "7.2.1", "rests_on": ["tea:tiruvaymoli:7.2.1"], "stage": "advanced (bridal love)", "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:andal-wedding-dream", "lineage": "lin:alvar", "kind": "vision", "description": "Āṇṭāḷ dreams her wedding to the Lord: the procession of a thousand elephants, the canopy, the rites, the circling of the fire.", "source": "src:nacciyar-tirumoli", "ref": "6", "rests_on": ["tea:nacciyar-tirumoli:6"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:andal-merging-into-ranganatha", "lineage": "lin:alvar", "kind": "state", "description": "Brought as a bride to Śrīraṅgam, Āṇṭāḷ entered the image of Raṅganātha and was seen no more.", "source": "src:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati", "ref": "Āṇṭāḷ", "rests_on": ["tea:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati:andal"], "stage": "the tradition's account", "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:tiruppan-feet-to-face-vision", "lineage": "lin:alvar", "kind": "vision", "description": "Carried into the sanctum, Tiruppāṇ saw the Lord part by part from his feet to his eyes, declared that his eyes would see nothing else, and merged into the Lord.", "source": "src:amalanatipiran", "ref": "1-10", "rests_on": ["tea:amalanatipiran:2-9", "tea:amalanatipiran:10", "tea:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati:tiruppan"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:kulasekhara-ramayana-absorption", "lineage": "lin:alvar", "kind": "state", "description": "Absorbed in the Rāmāyaṇa recital, King Kulaśekhara took Rāma's battle as present and ordered his army to Rāma's aid.", "source": "src:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati", "ref": "Kulaśekhara", "rests_on": ["tea:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati:kulasekhara"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:tirumankai-mantra-whispered", "lineage": "lin:alvar", "kind": "sound", "description": "The Lord, disguised as a bridegroom, whispered the eight-syllable mantra into Tirumaṅkai's ear; he broke at once into the hymn of the name.", "source": "src:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati", "ref": "Tirumaṅkai", "rests_on": ["tea:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati:tirumankai", "tea:periya-tirumoli:1.1.1"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:kumbakonam-image-rising", "lineage": "lin:alvar", "kind": "sign", "description": "When Tirumaḻicai asked the reclining Lord at Kuṭantai to rise and speak, the image began to rise and remains half-risen.", "source": "src:tiruccanta-viruttam", "ref": "61", "rests_on": ["tea:tiruccanta-viruttam:61"], "stage": "the tradition's account", "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:nathamuni-vision-of-nammalvar", "lineage": "lin:visistadvaita", "kind": "vision", "description": "After reciting the Kaṇṇinuṇ Ciṟuttāmpu twelve thousand times in yogic absorption at Kurukūr, Nāthamuni saw Nammāḻvār, who gave him the four thousand hymns and their meaning.", "source": "src:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati", "ref": "Nāthamuni", "rests_on": ["tea:guruparampara-prabhavam-arayirappati:nathamuni"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:nbs-signs-of-love", "lineage": "lin:bhakti-sastra", "kind": "bodily", "description": "The one-pointed devotees speak to one another with choked voices, bristling hair and tears.", "source": "src:narada-bhakti-sutra", "ref": "68", "rests_on": ["tea:narada-bhakti-sutra:67-71"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:nbs-intoxicated-still-self-delighting", "lineage": "lin:bhakti-sastra", "kind": "state", "description": "Knowing love, one becomes intoxicated, becomes still, becomes one who delights in the self; one desires, grieves over and hates nothing.", "source": "src:narada-bhakti-sutra", "ref": "5-6", "rests_on": ["tea:narada-bhakti-sutra:5", "tea:narada-bhakti-sutra:6"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:nbs-mute-tasting", "lineage": "lin:bhakti-sastra", "kind": "state", "description": "Love is indescribable, like a mute's tasting; increasing every moment, unbroken, subtlest, of the nature of experience; one sees, hears, speaks and thinks only of him.", "source": "src:narada-bhakti-sutra", "ref": "51-55", "rests_on": ["tea:narada-bhakti-sutra:51-54", "tea:narada-bhakti-sutra:55"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:radha-viraha-signs", "lineage": "lin:jagannatha", "kind": "bodily", "description": "Rādhā in separation: the bed of flowers burns her, moonlight is fire, she draws his image and wastes away, as her friend tells Kṛṣṇa.", "source": "src:gita-govinda", "ref": "4-6", "rests_on": ["tea:gita-govinda:4-6"], "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "phn:jayadeva-line-written-by-krsna", "lineage": "lin:jagannatha", "kind": "sign", "description": "When Jayadeva hesitated to write that Kṛṣṇa asks for Rādhā's foot on his head, Kṛṣṇa himself, in Jayadeva's form, came while he bathed and wrote the line.", "source": "src:gita-govinda", "ref": "10 (aṣṭapadī 19)", "rests_on": ["tea:gita-govinda:10.astapadi-19"], "stage": "the tradition's account", "coverage": ["A9", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
